- V8 pass rule: a matching is an exact `(sku, wh, qty)` triple. Quantity must match, and an entry with no expiries passes because it has nothing to notify. Tell me if a notification should match on `(sku, wh)` only, or if an entry with no expiries should fail.
- V8 and V9 "measured" values: V8 reports entry indices, since its entries have no key. V7 and V9 report the warehouse or supplier name, falling back to `None` for malformed entries. This follows the existing convention of reporting keys or indices.
- Type strictness: capacity, max_units and reliability must be real ints. Bools and floats fail, as do missing fields.
